    "result": "Excellent! The fix is complete and working. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Issue:** The `frai gate init --ci` command through the frai CLI was not passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI, so the GitHub Actions workflow file was not being created.\n\n**Root Cause:** When the `frai` CLI delegated to `frai-gate` using `spawnSync()`, the arguments were not being extracted correctly from Commander.js. The original code attempted to use variadic arguments with `.command('gate [args...]')` but didn't properly extract them from the command handler parameters.\n\n**Solution:** Changed the argument extraction in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to directly extract remaining arguments from `process.argv` by:\n1. Finding the index of `'gate'` in `process.argv`\n2. Taking all arguments after that index\n3. Passing them to `spawnSync()` which spawns the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Result:** \n- `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md` (the spec template)\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)\n- The fix maintains backward compatibility with `frai gate init` (without `--ci`)\n- The package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
